WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.320 --> 00:00:04.610
Legends about the end of the world often come
with the sounds of thundering hooves, and

00:00:04.610 --> 00:00:06.580
the approach of Four Horsemen.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:07.580
War.

00:00:07.580 --> 00:00:08.580
Famine.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:09.580
Pestilence.

00:00:09.580 --> 00:00:10.580
Death.

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:14.059
They will descend on the world and usher in
the end of days.

00:00:14.059 --> 00:00:19.430
It’s a terrifying idea, these horsemen bringing
darkness and decay wherever they go, as the

00:00:19.430 --> 00:00:21.940
world collapses all around them.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:26.609
We all hope that we’ll never see the day
that the Four Horsemen come.

00:00:26.609 --> 00:00:30.670
Unfortunately, some unlucky people out there
have already encountered their own version

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:36.940
of the Horsemen of the Apocalypse, shadowy
riders with inhuman strength that follow disaster,

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:39.399
destruction, and untold suffering.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:44.781
The SCP Foundation came across a series of
journal entries written by Dave Harkand, an

00:00:44.781 --> 00:00:50.600
infantryman in the British Expeditionary Force
during World War I. That first World War was

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:57.149
a nightmare for all who fought in it, a sea
of bloodshed and gunfire, young men crouched

00:00:57.149 --> 00:01:01.949
terrified in foxholes and wondering when death
would finally come for them.

00:01:01.949 --> 00:01:07.960
The horrors of war are notable, but not exactly
the sort of thing the SCP Foundation preoccupies

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.330
itself with.

00:01:09.330 --> 00:01:15.330
So what was so captivating, so specifically
terrible, about Dave Harkand’s journals?

00:01:15.330 --> 00:01:20.250
They described his experiences over the course
of The Battle of the Somme, and an anomaly

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:24.880
he encountered there that was unlike anything
he had ever seen.

00:01:24.880 --> 00:01:30.470
No military training, no combat experience,
could have prepared him for what was waiting,

00:01:30.470 --> 00:01:32.649
hiding in the fog of war.

00:01:32.649 --> 00:01:37.570
His first journal entry began on a lighthearted
note, or as lighthearted as one can be in

00:01:37.570 --> 00:01:39.200
the face of combat.

00:01:39.200 --> 00:01:43.549
“June 27th, 1916
Finally arrived at the front!

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:47.380
I picked up this little journal while I was
in Paris, figured I might as well keep record

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:49.270
of my heroics on the battlefield.

00:01:49.270 --> 00:01:52.350
Quite chuffed to finally be in action, though
it seems I'm the only one.

00:01:52.350 --> 00:01:56.220
Most of these blokes have been fighting for
a couple months now, and they look downright

00:01:56.220 --> 00:01:57.220
dreadful.

00:01:57.220 --> 00:02:00.920
Mud all over the uniform, and their faces
are so pale, look like they haven't eaten

00:02:00.920 --> 00:02:02.340
or slept for months.”

00:02:02.340 --> 00:02:07.650
A few days later, he began to hear stirrings
amongst his fellow soldiers, and strange sounds

00:02:07.650 --> 00:02:09.420
that rocked their barracks.

00:02:09.420 --> 00:02:13.960
He described the first unsettling incident:
“July 2nd, 1916

00:02:13.960 --> 00:02:16.000
Woke in the early hours of the morning.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:20.550
Ground was shaking, damn near shook me out
into the muck on the dugout floor.

00:02:20.550 --> 00:02:23.990
Poor blokes in the bunks on the other side
looked liked they had seen a ghoul.

00:02:23.990 --> 00:02:27.250
Pair of Northern Irish lads from Kitchener’s
Armies if I remember right.

00:02:27.250 --> 00:02:31.460
Kept muttering about a Nuckatee?...Were both
gripping a gold crucifix.

00:02:31.460 --> 00:02:35.260
Was about to lay my head back down and get
a wink of shuteye when I ended up scrambling

00:02:35.260 --> 00:02:36.260
into the mud.

00:02:36.260 --> 00:02:38.080
Loudest damn thing I'd ever heard.

00:02:38.080 --> 00:02:42.570
Thought it was the Hun Artillery bout to mark
us with a whizz-bang, only problem was, never

00:02:42.570 --> 00:02:43.910
did get the bang.

00:02:43.910 --> 00:02:46.530
This morning asked our brass hat about the
Artillery barrage.

00:02:46.530 --> 00:02:50.490
Gave me a funny look, and asked what the bloody
hell I was talking about.”

00:02:50.490 --> 00:02:53.820
The next day, Dave went searching for the
source of the loud sound.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:58.850
He didn’t find any evidence of artillery,
but instead found something he had never seen

00:02:58.850 --> 00:02:59.850
before.

00:02:59.850 --> 00:03:03.060
It was a crater, shaped like a giant horse’s
hoof.

00:03:03.060 --> 00:03:07.900
He brushed it off as just another oddity of
the battlefield, a bit strange but nothing

00:03:07.900 --> 00:03:09.510
to be concerned about.

00:03:09.510 --> 00:03:12.140
There were more important things at hand,
anyway.

00:03:12.140 --> 00:03:18.090
The next day, he finally saw combat first-hand,
and things only got more bizarre and frightening.

00:03:18.090 --> 00:03:22.380
“July 3rd, 1916
Huns made a push today, first time they've

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:23.990
moved in our region.

00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.480
First time I'd ever seen combat.

00:03:25.480 --> 00:03:27.370
It's not romantic and adventurous.

00:03:27.370 --> 00:03:29.430
It's terrifying, and deadly.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:33.360
My hands can't stop shaking, already messed
up the chit once.

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:37.680
The Huns had our outfit up against a wall,
damn near overran us, didn't help that it

00:03:37.680 --> 00:03:41.270
rained the night before making our fox hole
filled to the brim with muck.

00:03:41.270 --> 00:03:45.240
One of the Fritz came right at me…just…I
put one right between his eyes.

00:03:45.240 --> 00:03:49.240
Fell right at the edge of the trench, and
had to look him in the eyes, poor lad couldn't

00:03:49.240 --> 00:03:51.640
have been more than 17 or 18.

00:03:51.640 --> 00:03:53.620
Martin, one of those Irish lads, is gone.

00:03:53.620 --> 00:03:57.640
Was unlike anything I'd ever seen, one moment
he's standing shooting at the Huns, all of

00:03:57.640 --> 00:03:59.900
the sudden, the mud starts boiling.

00:03:59.900 --> 00:04:04.240
Fore anyone can react, Mud just flies everywhere,
everyone else is suddenly knocked down off

00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:05.240
their feet.

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:07.030
I look up, and he’s just gone.

00:04:07.030 --> 00:04:08.730
Wasn't even body parts left.

00:04:08.730 --> 00:04:13.160
Haven't told anyone…but I'd swear that there
was bones coming up from underneath him right

00:04:13.160 --> 00:04:14.640
before the mud went flying.

00:04:14.640 --> 00:04:19.130
His mate, Brendan, was digging in the mud
for hours, looking for the crucifix.”

00:04:19.130 --> 00:04:22.390
Martin’s body was never found, no matter
how they searched.

00:04:22.390 --> 00:04:26.680
A little over a week later, things got even
worse.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:31.990
“July 14th &amp; 15th, 1916
Huns tried to push this morning in the rain.

00:04:31.990 --> 00:04:36.030
I was in the machine gun nest with Brendan,
the other Irish chap in my unit.

00:04:36.030 --> 00:04:40.600
They kept coming and coming, and getting stuck
in the mud, and I just kept shooting.

00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:41.600
Sun is rising.

00:04:41.600 --> 00:04:45.060
I'm on watch till 8, at least that's what
the Brasshat said.

00:04:45.060 --> 00:04:48.450
I've started losing track of how much times
been passing.

00:04:48.450 --> 00:04:50.010
There's something out there.

00:04:50.010 --> 00:04:52.660
Something lurking out in the mud and dead
Huns.

00:04:52.660 --> 00:04:56.250
Nearly dozed off last night, listening to
the moans of the blighty wounded stuck out

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:57.720
in No-man's land.

00:04:57.720 --> 00:04:59.860
Poor souls got left behind.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:03.080
Saw something out of the edge of my vision,
something big.

00:05:03.080 --> 00:05:08.190
Couldn't quite make it out, it was much darker
than usual, overcast sky was obscuring the

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:09.190
full moon.

00:05:09.190 --> 00:05:13.880
Heard a couple of screams, but whatever it
was, was gone before my flare hit the sky.”

00:05:13.880 --> 00:05:18.250
This would not be Dave’s last sighting of
the large, dark figure.

00:05:18.250 --> 00:05:22.510
This mysterious shadow would appear again,
several days later.

00:05:22.510 --> 00:05:24.330
And there would be more of them.

00:05:24.330 --> 00:05:28.940
“July 30th, 1916
I've been seeing them at the edge of my vision,

00:05:28.940 --> 00:05:30.490
ever since that first night.

00:05:30.490 --> 00:05:34.650
They're huge, but they move so damn fast that
they're gone before I can get a clear look.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.550
Or at least, that's how it was mucking out
until today.

00:05:37.550 --> 00:05:41.030
Thick fog and mist rolled in this morning,
blanketed everything.

00:05:41.030 --> 00:05:43.570
We figured the Huns might use it to launch
another push.

00:05:43.570 --> 00:05:46.340
Bastards have been pushing non-stop since
the 20th.

00:05:46.340 --> 00:05:50.290
Saw it, through the fog, looked like a shadow,
hiding in the mist.

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:55.960
Some sort of Horse like creature, with a something
dragging along the ground, and a giant lump

00:05:55.960 --> 00:05:59.200
where the rider would sit…cept the lump
started moving.

00:05:59.200 --> 00:06:02.060
Could have sworn it was a person, or something
that looked like a person.

00:06:02.060 --> 00:06:06.580
Sat up, and the things dragging along the
ground reached out in front of it and picked

00:06:06.580 --> 00:06:10.990
up something, thought it was a couple dead
Jerry's…until they started squirming.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:13.330
I'll never forget the noise it made.

00:06:13.330 --> 00:06:15.670
Louder than a banshee, shrill and twisted.

00:06:15.670 --> 00:06:17.490
It looked right at me.

00:06:17.490 --> 00:06:20.030
Two pairs of red glowing orbs.”

00:06:20.030 --> 00:06:24.550
Two weeks after meeting eyes with this chilling
apparition, Dave wrote a short note in his

00:06:24.550 --> 00:06:26.370
journal:
“August 5th

00:06:26.370 --> 00:06:27.400
Brendan calls them Nuckelavees.

00:06:27.400 --> 00:06:29.690
Won't tell me much more than that.

00:06:29.690 --> 00:06:33.250
Beginning to understand why all these blokes
looked so terrified when I first arrived.”

00:06:33.250 --> 00:06:37.350
It wasn’t until another week had passed
that Dave would truly begin to understand

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.150
just what kind of monster he was up against.

00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:44.310
Not the enemy soldiers, but something far
more horrible.

00:06:44.310 --> 00:06:45.380
Something inhuman.

00:06:45.380 --> 00:06:48.010
“August 13th
Bloody hell.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:49.010
They're nightmares.

00:06:49.010 --> 00:06:53.740
Been on watch two nights in a row, one just…appeared
right there, right in front of me.

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:56.250
20 feet, had to be at least 20 feet away.

00:06:56.250 --> 00:06:57.840
Towered into the sky.

00:06:57.840 --> 00:07:01.760
Got my flare to go off in time to see it pick
up a couple wounded Jerry's in the mud.

00:07:01.760 --> 00:07:03.210
They don't have bloody skin.

00:07:03.210 --> 00:07:05.250
There's just muscle, and fat.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:09.080
The thing on its back…wasn't human, no way
could it be human.

00:07:09.080 --> 00:07:13.110
Had no skin either, no legs, just merged straight
into the horse at the stomach.

00:07:13.110 --> 00:07:17.840
I took a couple shots at it with my rifle…did
absolutely nothing, like I was shooting it

00:07:17.840 --> 00:07:19.180
with a sling shot.

00:07:19.180 --> 00:07:22.740
It stopped soon as my flare reached its highest
point, and turned.

00:07:22.740 --> 00:07:27.010
Looked straight down at me, both the horse
and the…thing on its back.

00:07:27.010 --> 00:07:28.040
It smiled.”

00:07:28.040 --> 00:07:32.210
He tried to talk to his superiors, tried to
warn of the horrors he was seeing and the

00:07:32.210 --> 00:07:35.830
danger he felt they posed, but they wouldn’t
listen.

00:07:35.830 --> 00:07:38.310
Night after night, the creatures came back.

00:07:38.310 --> 00:07:42.800
“August 17th 1916
Been assigned night watch the past four nights

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:43.800
straight.

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:45.260
Tried to tell the brass hat about the nuckelavees.

00:07:45.260 --> 00:07:46.650
Didn't believe me.

00:07:46.650 --> 00:07:48.570
Said it was the shell shock playing with my
head.

00:07:48.570 --> 00:07:50.730
Had to put a sock in it, and keep on.

00:07:50.730 --> 00:07:52.860
It keeps coming back.

00:07:52.860 --> 00:07:53.990
Every night.

00:07:53.990 --> 00:07:56.270
Same spot, 20 feet in front of me.

00:07:56.270 --> 00:07:58.860
Picks up wounded Jerry's, turns and looks…and
then it's gone.

00:07:58.860 --> 00:08:01.440
It's playing with me, I'm sure of it.

00:08:01.440 --> 00:08:02.650
Last night there was another one too.

00:08:02.650 --> 00:08:05.680
Four of those things on its back, did the
same damn thing.”

00:08:05.680 --> 00:08:09.750
A few days later, Dave spotted something that
made his blood run cold.

00:08:09.750 --> 00:08:10.800
“7:00 A.M.

00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:14.930
August 20th 1916
Jerry's made a big push yesterday.

00:08:14.930 --> 00:08:17.540
Rained two days ago, all day, so the muck
was deep.

00:08:17.540 --> 00:08:20.110
We were on the machinegun again in the pillbox.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:24.419
So many of them in no-man's land last night,
couldn't tell the dead from the living.

00:08:24.419 --> 00:08:25.940
Haven't slept in six days.

00:08:25.940 --> 00:08:27.220
There were five tonight.

00:08:27.220 --> 00:08:31.030
Three of them had more than one of those…things
on their back.

00:08:31.030 --> 00:08:34.389
The one that keeps coming back…dropped something.

00:08:34.389 --> 00:08:36.110
Saw it shine in the flare light.

00:08:36.110 --> 00:08:37.110
10:00 A.M.

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:40.479
August 20th 1916
Went out into the mud where it appears every

00:08:40.479 --> 00:08:41.479
night.

00:08:41.479 --> 00:08:43.469
Found Martin's crucifix and tin hat.”

00:08:43.469 --> 00:08:46.470
Whatever this thing was, it had taken Martin.

00:08:46.470 --> 00:08:48.870
It seemed to want Dave to know that, too.

00:08:48.870 --> 00:08:52.390
It left behind Martin’s lost things for
him to find.

00:08:52.390 --> 00:08:53.740
As if it was gloating.

00:08:53.740 --> 00:08:56.510
As if it already knew that it had won.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:09:00.890
“August 20th 1916
They're getting bold, saw one out in broad

00:09:00.890 --> 00:09:01.890
daylight.

00:09:01.890 --> 00:09:03.290
Pretty sure it was the same one.

00:09:03.290 --> 00:09:06.270
Buried itself in the mud, just lying there…waiting.

00:09:06.270 --> 00:09:08.330
We're going over the top at three.

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:12.450
There are more out there now…all doing the
same thing…god help us.”

00:09:12.450 --> 00:09:17.690
Dave Harkand was declared Missing in Action
on August 20, 1916, following an attempted

00:09:17.690 --> 00:09:20.520
counterattack against the German forces.

00:09:20.520 --> 00:09:24.670
Another soldier from his unit, Brendan O’Malley,
was also reported Missing in Action on the

00:09:24.670 --> 00:09:25.670
same day.

00:09:25.670 --> 00:09:29.600
Though Dave’s body was never recovered,
his journal was found 20 feet away from the

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.420
edge of the German trenches two months later.

00:09:32.420 --> 00:09:36.670
Poor Dave Harkand had no idea what he, and
the rest of his fellow soldiers, encountered

00:09:36.670 --> 00:09:37.670
out there.

00:09:37.670 --> 00:09:42.180
He didn’t live to learn more, but he came
face to face with SCP-3456.

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:51.070
SCP-3456 is not one being, but rather a group
of quadrupeds that vaguely resemble horses.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.760
From a distance, their silhouette looks like
that of a horse with a human riding on its

00:09:54.760 --> 00:09:55.760
back.

00:09:55.760 --> 00:10:00.420
However, once the observer gets closer, they
will notice some disturbing differences.

00:10:00.420 --> 00:10:03.500
These creatures do not look like any ordinary
horse.

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:08.970
They are smooth and hairless, with translucent
skin and three-toed hooves.

00:10:08.970 --> 00:10:12.220
Anyone unfortunate enough to get close to
one of these creatures will be able to see

00:10:12.220 --> 00:10:15.970
through their skin to the blood vessels and
muscle underneath.

00:10:15.970 --> 00:10:19.980
They will also notice that there is no rider
perched atop the creature’s back at all.

00:10:19.980 --> 00:10:26.190
The humanoid shape is a part of the creature’s
body, an extension of them, fused to its back.

00:10:26.190 --> 00:10:30.820
The humanoid figure consists of a pair of
long arms, which drag along the ground as

00:10:30.820 --> 00:10:32.940
the creature moves, and a head.

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:38.630
The arms end in sharpened bones rather than
fingers, and the head has mostly human features,

00:10:38.630 --> 00:10:41.750
with the exception of a hole where the nose
should be.

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:46.230
The creatures vary greatly in size, with the
largest on record measuring at a height of

00:10:46.230 --> 00:10:48.670
30 meters and a width of 15.

00:10:48.670 --> 00:10:53.420
They appear to be invulnerable, at least when
it comes to any traditional human weaponry

00:10:53.420 --> 00:10:56.160
they have currently been exposed to.

00:10:56.160 --> 00:11:01.990
Gunfire, explosives, swords and arrows, and
even nuclear blasts seem to have no effect.

00:11:01.990 --> 00:11:06.990
If you happen to get a look at one of these
bulletproof abominations in person, then I

00:11:06.990 --> 00:11:07.990
am so sorry.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:10.370
You are as good as gone.

00:11:10.370 --> 00:11:15.230
Because once you’ve seen one of these creatures,
they have also seen you, and they will not

00:11:15.230 --> 00:11:17.670
stop until they have taken you.

00:11:17.670 --> 00:11:23.170
They will track you, stalk you, hide buried
in mud and nestled in bushes.

00:11:23.170 --> 00:11:27.110
They will wait for the opportune moment, and
they will reach out with their unnaturally

00:11:27.110 --> 00:11:33.330
long arms, smiling with no lips as their blood
red eyes burn like hellfire, and you will

00:11:33.330 --> 00:11:35.149
disappear forever.

00:11:35.149 --> 00:11:39.230
They will travel far beyond the site where
they first appeared, until they have finally

00:11:39.230 --> 00:11:40.880
captured their prey.

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:44.490
This isn’t an SCP-096 situation, either.

00:11:44.490 --> 00:11:46.670
They aren’t punishing you for seeing their
face.

00:11:46.670 --> 00:11:51.500
They want to be seen, and will go out of their
way to show themselves to people until they

00:11:51.500 --> 00:11:53.940
have captured as many as they want.

00:11:53.940 --> 00:11:59.560
No one knows what becomes of SCP-3456’s
victims, but they are never seen again.

00:11:59.560 --> 00:12:04.680
Though items once belonging to the missing
people may resurface, their bodies are never

00:12:04.680 --> 00:12:05.680
found.

00:12:05.680 --> 00:12:11.850
There is only one way to escape from SCP-3456,
and that is to find and cross a body of fresh

00:12:11.850 --> 00:12:12.850
water.

00:12:12.850 --> 00:12:18.320
For reasons unknown, the entities are unable
or unwilling to cross rivers, streams, and

00:12:18.320 --> 00:12:19.320
lakes.

00:12:19.320 --> 00:12:23.370
The Foundation first discovered this during
an operation in Iraq, in which several agents

00:12:23.370 --> 00:12:26.680
encountered a group of SCP-3456 manifestations.

00:12:26.680 --> 00:12:31.660
They fled from the monsters, and quickly retreated
across the Tigris river.

00:12:31.660 --> 00:12:35.480
Once they had reached the other side, they
saw that the creatures had not followed them

00:12:35.480 --> 00:12:36.890
onto the bridge.

00:12:36.890 --> 00:12:42.270
Instead, they remained at the riverbank on
the other side, watching, and waiting.

00:12:42.270 --> 00:12:47.390
This was quickly noted, and added to potential
containment procedures, though the exact reason

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:51.930
for SCP-3456’s dislike of fresh water is
currently unknown.

00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:56.780
In Dave Harkland’s journals, his fellow
soldier described the creatures as “Nuckelavees,”

00:12:56.780 --> 00:12:59.350
but would not elaborate beyond that.

00:12:59.350 --> 00:13:01.180
So what is a Nuckelavee?

00:13:01.180 --> 00:13:05.620
The word refers to a creature from the waters
of Orkney, a group of islands on the northern

00:13:05.620 --> 00:13:07.330
coast of Scotland.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:11.731
Their name is thought to come from an Orcadian
word meaning “Devil of the Sea,” and they

00:13:11.731 --> 00:13:14.779
truly are like something out of hell.

00:13:14.779 --> 00:13:19.190
These creatures are native to the ocean, and
supposedly take on another form when in their

00:13:19.190 --> 00:13:23.380
natural habitat, but no one knows what they
truly look like.

00:13:23.380 --> 00:13:28.660
On land, the creature is a hybrid of man and
horse, with a large snout like that of a pig,

00:13:28.660 --> 00:13:32.110
and a single red eye that burns like the embers
of a fire.

00:13:32.110 --> 00:13:38.339
It has no hair or skin, just raw, tissue and
bone dripping black blood.

00:13:38.339 --> 00:13:43.060
Everything about the creature is malicious
and deadly, intended to bring harm and calamity

00:13:43.060 --> 00:13:44.440
to humans.

00:13:44.440 --> 00:13:49.810
Even its breath is toxic, thought to cause
disease, plague, and the death of crops.

00:13:49.810 --> 00:13:54.470
As they are native to the ocean, they detest
fresh water, and will not cross it even in

00:13:54.470 --> 00:13:56.090
pursuit of their prey.

00:13:56.090 --> 00:13:58.690
They will also not appear when it is raining.

00:13:58.690 --> 00:14:02.350
In the legends of the Nuckelavee, they do
have a natural enemy.

00:14:02.350 --> 00:14:07.029
A creature from Orcadian folklore known as
the Mither of the Sea is said to have the

00:14:07.029 --> 00:14:10.779
power to keep the monsters from coming ashore
during the Summer months.

00:14:10.779 --> 00:14:16.200
The Mither, or Mother, is a benevolent force
of nature, giving warmth to the oceans and

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.340
life to the beings of the water and the land.

00:14:19.340 --> 00:14:24.690
Though SCP-3456 has appeared during the Summer
months, it has never been spotted in the Orkney

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:27.240
region during this time of year.

00:14:27.240 --> 00:14:32.330
Perhaps this is a coincidence, but some Foundation
researchers have proposed a research expedition

00:14:32.330 --> 00:14:36.080
to the area in order to look for the kindly
ocean spirit.

00:14:36.080 --> 00:14:39.290
So far, this proposal has been denied.

00:14:39.290 --> 00:14:44.630
SCP-3456 is classified as Keter, and there
is currently no way to effectively contain

00:14:44.630 --> 00:14:45.630
it.

00:14:45.630 --> 00:14:49.760
All previous attempts to contain or to neutralize
the horsemen have failed, though the Foundation

00:14:49.760 --> 00:14:52.380
is always looking for new methods to attempt.

00:14:52.380 --> 00:14:56.779
Currently, any personnel who see the horsemen
will be given Class G amnestics at a treatment

00:14:56.779 --> 00:15:01.770
center located within one kilometer of a freshwater
stream, river, or lake.

00:15:01.770 --> 00:15:06.279
All references to the horsemen have been scrubbed
from historical records, and any sightings

00:15:06.279 --> 00:15:10.950
are to be blamed on PTSD, shock, and trauma-induced
hysteria.

00:15:10.950 --> 00:15:17.089
Areas that are likely to attract SCP-3456,
such as war zones and areas impacted by natural

00:15:17.089 --> 00:15:20.600
disasters, are to be heavily monitored by
the Foundation.

00:15:20.600 --> 00:15:25.590
In the event of a disaster, Foundation personnel
will be sent to help with evacuation in order

00:15:25.590 --> 00:15:30.540
to get all civilians away from SCP-3456 as
quickly as possible.

00:15:30.540 --> 00:15:33.560
So what is SCP-3456?

00:15:33.560 --> 00:15:37.860
Is it the dreaded Nuckelavee from folktales
and whispered fireside warnings?

00:15:37.860 --> 00:15:42.830
There are some notable differences between
the stories and what the Foundation encountered.

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:47.930
SCP-3456 does not seem to have come from the
ocean, nor is it limited to only appearing

00:15:47.930 --> 00:15:49.350
around Orkney.

00:15:49.350 --> 00:15:54.899
These beasts seem to manifest from thin air,
and disappear the same way when their nasty

00:15:54.899 --> 00:15:56.010
work is done.

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:59.960
But, folklore and passing down stories often
distorts things.

00:15:59.960 --> 00:16:03.930
Details change, and others are added or left
out.

00:16:03.930 --> 00:16:08.120
In the original stories, the Nuckelavee was
thought to be the cause of famines, plagues,

00:16:08.120 --> 00:16:09.579
and disasters.

00:16:09.579 --> 00:16:15.110
Perhaps it was simply drawn to these events,
lured there by the scent of pure human misery.

00:16:15.110 --> 00:16:21.240
Perhaps the Nuckelavee is not just similar
to SCP-3456, but the two are one and the same.

00:16:21.240 --> 00:16:24.820
Or perhaps they are something entirely different.

00:16:24.820 --> 00:16:29.070
Whatever the case may be, there is nothing
we can do to stop them.

00:16:29.070 --> 00:16:35.390
War, famine, pestilence, and death are everywhere,
they are inevitable and unfortunate parts

00:16:35.390 --> 00:16:36.790
of life on earth.

00:16:36.790 --> 00:16:43.170
So, it seems, are these deadly riders, these
monsters that are neither horse nor man, but

00:16:43.170 --> 00:16:45.399
still somehow both.

00:16:45.399 --> 00:16:51.470
Every time we wage war, every time disaster
strikes, they will come to watch, to pick

00:16:51.470 --> 00:16:54.010
through the rubble, and to smile.

00:16:54.010 --> 00:16:57.769
Maybe, we don’t need to dread the coming
of the Horsemen of the Apocalypse.

00:16:57.769 --> 00:17:00.160
They are already here.

00:17:00.160 --> 00:17:06.129
Now go check out “Waldo Finds You - SCP-4885
- Find Him” and “The Secret at the Bottom

00:17:06.129 --> 00:17:11.100
of SCP-087 - EXPLAINED” for more monstrous
finds from the SCP Foundation!

